    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1180">

                <pb facs="1061" n="747" sameAs="frus:frus1914Supp/pg747"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 125.0067/17</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Turkey</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Morgenthau</hi>)</head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1914-11-17T18:00:00-05:00">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">November 17, 1914, 6 p.m.</hi>
                    </date>
                </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">[Telegram]</p>
                <p>37. Your 21, November 12, 3 p.m., received to-day. You may strongly protest
                    against the Turkish authorities searching all consulates in charge of American
                    representatives and everything therein <pb facs="1062" n="748" xml:id="pg748"/>
                    except archives. You may, if not too late, instruct American consular
                    representatives to be present unofficially in order that they may later give
                    testimony as to the acts of the Turkish authorities.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
